---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config';
---
<Base title="About">
  <header class="article-head"><h1>About this journal</h1></header>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>Most writing about AI is about models and chips. This journal is about the part underneath: the power, the grid connection, the transformer, the rack, the cooling loop, and the supply chains that decide whether any of it gets built on time.</p>
    <p>That layer is where the physics is slow, the data is public, and the constraint is real. It is also the part that almost nobody explains in plain language.</p>
    <p>Each piece here starts with a one-line version anyone can understand, then goes as deep as the subject needs. Where I have a view, I say what would prove it wrong.</p>
    <h2>Who writes it</h2>
    <p>I'm {SITE.author}, a civil engineer by training (UCL MEng, 2025) who moved into investment research. I spent time as an Investment Analyst at Cross Labs / Cross Compass in Tokyo, and since mid-2026 I've published independent research on power, grid connection and digital infrastructure, with a model behind every call and a dated record of how each one turned out.</p>
    <p>Engineering taught me to respect what physically has to be true. Research taught me to say what I think will happen and be marked on it. This journal is where the two meet.</p>
    <p class="sources">Everything here is personal research, not investment advice. Reach me at <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a> or on <a href={SITE.linkedin}>LinkedIn</a>.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
